    "pages_read_directly": {
      "https://www.example.com/blog/reduce-no-shows/": "Nine tactics: automatic reminders 24 hours and 2 hours before the visit; a one-tap link to confirm or reschedule in every reminder; a deposit for long or first-time appointments; a clear cancellation window (24 hours is the most common); a waitlist that fills freed slots; a follow-up message after a missed visit. Reminders are the first tactic because they catch clients who simply forgot.",
      "https://www.example.com/features/reminders/": "Reminders go out by SMS and email. You choose when they go: 48 hours, 24 hours or 2 hours before. Each reminder carries the time, the address and a link to confirm, cancel or reschedule. The wording can be edited per service.",
      "https://www.example.com/industries/salons/": "Clients book 24/7 from your website, Instagram and Google. Reminders go out automatically, deposits can be taken for long services, and every stylist works from one shared calendar. Plans start at $19 a month for one staff member; the Business plan is $99 for up to 20.",
      "https://www.example.com/blog/appointment-reminder-templates/": "A good reminder text stays under 160 characters, names the business, gives the day and time, and ends with one action: reply C to confirm or tap the link to reschedule. The post has 14 templates for salons, clinics and studios.",
      "https://www.example.com/templates/cancellation-policy/": "Most salons ask for 24 hours' notice. The template sets a 24-hour window, a fee of 50% of the service price for late cancellations, the full price for no-shows, and one free late cancellation a year for regular clients. Show the policy at booking and in every reminder.",
      "https://www.example.com/blog/deposit-policy/": "Take the deposit by card when the client books online; the slot is held once it is paid. 20 to 50% of the service price is common, or a fixed amount for short services. The deposit comes off the final bill and is kept if the client cancels inside the cancellation window.",
      "https://www.example.com/blog/how-to-take-online-bookings/": "Setup takes four steps: add your services with prices and durations, set each staff member's working hours, connect the calendar you already use, and put the booking link on your website, your Instagram profile and your Google Business Profile.",
      "https://www.example.com/integrations/facebook/": "Add a Book now button to your Facebook page that opens your booking page. Clients pick a service, a staff member and a time, and the booking lands in the same calendar as every other booking."
    },
